ts; replace forms as PDFs if needed\\n- Schools updates: Update links and brief descriptions as needed\\n\\nRoles and permissions:\\n- 1–2 primary admins: manage site settings, member approvals, and structure\\n- 1–3 content editors: create/edit posts and pages (no access to billing)\\n- Residents: read-only access to member pages\\n\\nContact and privacy:\\n- Contact form submissions routed to the single HOA email address\\n- CAPTCHA/anti-spam enabled; SSL enabled site-wide\\n- Collect minimal PII (name, address, email) for access control and communications\\n- Simple privacy note explaining data usage for HOA purposes only\\n\\nAnalytics and monitoring:\\n- Use Squarespace Analytics for page views and traffic trends\\n- No third-party trackers required\\n\\nConstraints and non-requirements:\\n- No online payments on the site\\n- No complex calendar or RSVP features (simple posts only)\\n- Avoid custom code; use native Squarespace features to keep updates easy\\n\\nSuccess criteria (acceptance):\\n- All specified pages exist with correct visibility (public vs resident-only)\\n- A resident can request access and, after admin approval, sign in successfully\\n- A board editor can publish a News post in under 5 minutes without code\\n- Contact form successfully delivers to the HOA email and blocks obvious spam\\n- Legal Docs are readable/downloadable on desktop and mobile\\n\\nImplementation outline (high level):\\n- Configure Squarespace site with chosen template; connect existing domain\\n- Set up Member Areas and gated pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\n- Build Request Access form and admin approval workflow (manual add/invite)\\n- Create page structures and starter content; upload initial PDFs\\n- Configure Contact form routing; enable spam protection and SSL\\n- Invite board admins/editors; provide a 1-page quick-start guide for updates\\n\\nFuture optional enhancements (out of scope now):\\n- Event calendar and optional RSVPs\\n- Online dues payments 